// The macOS system interface: `libSystem`, Apple's only stable one (it has
// no stable system calls). Names and argument orders are the C library's,
// so the man pages document them, and the constants are Darwin's values,
// which often differ from Linux's (`O_CREAT` is `0x200`, `MAP_ANON`
// `0x1000`). C `int` is `@bit32`; `size_t`, `ssize_t`, `off_t` and `long`
// are `@bit_native`; `void *` is `ref unknown`; a path is a NUL-terminated
// byte string. A failed call returns `-1` (or null) and sets `errno()`.
//
// Every function here is listed in `toolchain/*-apple-darwin/libSystem.tbd`,
// the stub a native build links.

// Files and descriptors. `open` and `fcntl` are variadic in C: pass
// `open`'s mode (`@bit32`) only with `O_CREAT`.

open: extern function (path: ref @bit8, oflag: @bit32, ...) fd: @bit32
close: extern function (fildes: @bit32) result: @bit32
read: extern function (fildes: @bit32, buf: ref unknown, nbyte: @bit_native) result: @bit_native
write: extern function (fildes: @bit32, buf: ref unknown, nbyte: @bit_native) result: @bit_native
pread: extern function (fildes: @bit32, buf: ref unknown, nbyte: @bit_native, offset: @bit_native) result: @bit_native
pwrite: extern function (fildes: @bit32, buf: ref unknown, nbyte: @bit_native, offset: @bit_native) result: @bit_native
lseek: extern function (fildes: @bit32, offset: @bit_native, whence: @bit32) result: @bit_native
fsync: extern function (fildes: @bit32) result: @bit32
ftruncate: extern function (fildes: @bit32, length: @bit_native) result: @bit32
fcntl: extern function (fildes: @bit32, cmd: @bit32, ...) result: @bit32
dup: extern function (fildes: @bit32) result: @bit32
dup2: extern function (fildes: @bit32, fildes2: @bit32) result: @bit32
/// `fildes` is two `@bit32`s: the read end, then the write end.
pipe: extern function (fildes: ref unknown) result: @bit32
isatty: extern function (fildes: @bit32) result: @bit32

unlink: extern function (path: ref @bit8) result: @bit32
mkdir: extern function (path: ref @bit8, mode: @bit16) result: @bit32
rmdir: extern function (path: ref @bit8) result: @bit32
rename: extern function (old: ref @bit8, new: ref @bit8) result: @bit32
access: extern function (path: ref @bit8, mode: @bit32) result: @bit32
getcwd: extern function (buf: ref @bit8, size: @bit_native) result: ref @bit8
chdir: extern function (path: ref @bit8) result: @bit32
